/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Ethernet is a wired networking technology that enables data transfer between devices using cables. Initially developed in the 1970s by Xerox, Intel, and DEC, it became the IEEE 802.3 standard, providing scalable, high-speed, and secure communication. Today, Ethernet is the backbone of modern networking, connecting homes, businesses, data centers, and cloud environments.)
/Pg 8 0 R
/K [2]
>>
